O(log n) - Each iteration reduces the remaining search space by approximately half. Therefore, at most `O(log n)` iterations are performed, where `n `is `nums.size().`

**Space Complexity:**
O(1) - The algorithm uses only the variables `low, high, and mid`, so its auxiliary space complexity is `O(1)`.

